course: dictionary
lesson: 8042
title: Regional words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A region is an area of a country or of the world. Regional means to do with one particular area. A regional accent is the way people in one area say words, and it can sound different from the way people in another area speak.
explain: Read the clue in this sentence: «Most British people do not speak the "posh" BBC accent» and «the rest have regional accents.» The word rest tells you the ordinary accents are the regional ones, and they belong to particular places. So regional means to do with one area, not the whole country.
explain: Regional shows up in everyday life too. Regional news covers your own area, regional trains link towns close together, and in sport a regional final comes before the national one. When you meet the word regional, ask yourself: which area is this about?
fact: Regional means to do with a particular region.
fact: A region is an area of a country or of the world.
fact: Regional accents and dialects show where people come from, for example Geordie, Scouse, Cockney and Texan.
fact: «The vyshyvanka» is an embroidered shirt with regional patterns and colours, and Vyshyvanka Day is in May.
fact: It is often estimated that only about 2 or 3 in every 100 people speak the "posh" BBC accent naturally.
exercise: What does regional mean? | To do with sport only | To do with very old things | To do with the whole world at once | *To do with a particular area of a country or the world
exercise: «Most British people do not speak the "posh" BBC accent... the rest have regional accents.» What is a regional accent? | A type of train | *The way people in one area speak | A way of singing a song | A posh voice used only on the BBC
exercise: Which of these is an example of a regional difference? | The colour of a bicycle | *Different food and weather in two areas of one country | A number in a sum | Two people sharing the same birthday
test: The vyshyvanka has regional patterns and colours. What does regional tell you about those patterns? | They come from the whole world at once | *They come from a particular area | They are made of metal | They are the same in every country
test: In sport, which comes first? | *A regional final | A national final | The last game of the season | The final of a school quiz
exam: «Regional trains link towns.» What does regional mean here? | Trains that only carry food | Trains that go to the moon | *Trains that connect towns in one area | Trains that never stop
